  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">GHG emissions cap- setting guidelines for coal power subsector of the energy sector and cement subsector of the industry sector</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">GHG emissions cap- setting guidelines for coal power subsector of the energy sector and cement subsector of the industry sector</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">N/A</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">2 GHG emissions cap- setting guidelines for coal power subsector of the energy sector and cement subsector of the industry sector</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">the Climate Promise project continue to support carbon market implementation by providing technical assistance in the preparation of GHG emissions capsetting guidelines on coalfired powerplants. This guideline is indispensable by the Government of Indonesian, especially the Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources (MoEMR) because of the obligation to provide GHG emissions cap-setting for power plants if the sector will implement the carbon trading. This is in accordance with the mandate of regulations regarding Carbon Pricing in Indonesia and successfully facilitated to develop the Roadmap 2024 2060 for Emission Cap and Allowance and Guidelines for Carbon Pricing Mechanisms Implementation to hire consultant company</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tonnes of CO2 emissions avoided or reduced; Megawatts of renewable or low-emission energy capacity installed, generated or rehabilitated; Number of beneficiaries with new access to green/sustainable energy (disaggregated by: male, female, youth (15-24) and indigenous people)</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">The updated NDC submitted in 2021 pledges to reduce emissions from 2020-2030 by 29% (unconditional) up to 41% (conditional) against the 2030 business as usual scenario of 2.869 GtCO2e. Forest and land use and energy sectors account for about 97% of the total national commitment.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">11% reduction against business as usual (BAU) under unconditional mitigation scenario
15.5% against BAU under conditional mitigation scenario
-----------------------------
By 2025 and 2050, the primary energy supply mix as follows:
a) new and renewable energy at least 23% in 2025 and at least 31% in 2050;
b) oil should be less than 25% in 2025 and less than 20% in 2050;
c) coal should be minimum 30% in 2025 and minimum 25% in 2050; and
d) gas should be minimum 22% in 2025 and minimum 24% in 2050.

0.10% against BAU under unconditional mitigation scenario
0.11% against BAU under conditional mitigation scenario
0.32% against BAU under unconditional mitigation scenario
0.13% against BAU under conditional mitigation scenario

17.2% against BAU under unconditional mitigation scenario
24.5% against BAU under conditional mitigation scenario</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partial: actual reduction will be evaluated when ETS is in place.
Partial: actual reduction will be evaluated when ETS and other carbon pricing transactions take place.

UNDP provided technical support alignment to and technical implementation of Indonesia&#x2019;s Nationally Determined Contributions (NDC) and Long-Term Strategy for Low Carbon and Climate Resilience 2050 through, among others, Leveraging NDCs to Achieve Net-Zero Emissions and Climate-Resilient Development, in response to Climate Emergency Project, funded by the Japan Supplementary Budget as part of Climate Promise 2.0</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
